---
import ContentLayout from "../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import type { FaqItem } from "../../lib/seo";

const faqs: FaqItem[] = [
  { q: "What is a TDEE calculator?", a: "A TDEE calculator (Total Daily Energy Expenditure) finds your maintenance calories. Eat this amount to keep weight stable. Use our <a href='/tdee-calculator/'>TDEE calculator</a>." },
  { q: "How does a TDEE calculator work?", a: "It calculates BMR using Mifflin-St Jeor, then multiplies by activity level. Result is your maintenance calories for weight management." },
  { q: "Why is my TDEE calculator wrong?", a: "Common issues: overestimating activity, incorrect stats, or metabolic adaptation. Track weight to verify, then adjust." },
  { q: "Can I use TDEE calculator for weight loss?", a: "Yes. Subtract 250–500 from your <a href='/guides/maintenance-calorie-calculator/'>maintenance calories</a> for sustainable weight loss." },
];
---

<ContentLayout
  title="TDEE Calculator — Total Daily Energy Expenditure Explained"
  h1="TDEE Calculator"
  description="Free TDEE calculator finds your maintenance calories. Learn Total Daily Energy Expenditure, how it works, and use it for weight loss or gain goals."
  path="/resources/tdee-calculator/"
  category="Resources"
  categoryPath="/resources/"
  lead="Your TDEE is the calories you can eat to maintain weight. Calculate it here."
  updated="June 2026"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p>A <strong>TDEE calculator</strong> reveals your Total Daily Energy Expenditure—the calories you burn each day. This equals your <a href="/guides/maintenance-calorie-calculator/">maintenance calories</a>.</p>

  <h2>What TDEE means</h2>
  <p>TDEE = BMR + TEF + Activity EE. Simply: all calories burned in 24 hours.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Contribution</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>BMR (Basal Metabolic Rate)</td><td>60–70%</td></tr>
      <tr><td>TEF (Thermic Effect of Food)</td><td>~10%</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Exercise Activity</td><td>10–20%</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Non-exercise Activity (NEAT)</td><td>15–20%</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>How our TDEE calculator works</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Enter age, sex, height, weight</li>
    <li>Select activity level honestly</li>
    <li>Mifflin-St Jeor calculates BMR</li>
    <li>Activity factor creates TDEE</li>
    <li>Use <a href="/tdee-calculator/">our TDEE calculator</a> for instant results</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>TDEE calculator activity levels explained</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Description</th><th>Multiplier</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Sedentary</td><td>Desk job, minimal exercise</td><td>1.2</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Lightly Active</td><td>1–3 workouts/week</td><td>1.375</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Moderately Active</td><td>3–5 workouts/week</td><td>1.55</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Very Active</td><td>6–7 workouts/week</td><td>1.725</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Extra Active</td><td>Athlete + physical job</td><td>1.9</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>TDEE calculator example</h2>
  <p>30-year-old man, 180 cm, 80 kg:</p>
  <pre>BMR = 10 × 80 + 6.25 × 180 - 5 × 30 + 5 = 1,820
TDEE (Moderate) = 1,820 × 1.55 = 2,821 calories</pre>
  <p>This is his <a href="/guides/maintenance-calorie-calculator/">maintenance calorie calculator</a> number.</p>

  <h2>Common TDEE calculator mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Choosing "athlete" without training intensely</li>
    <li>Using outdated weight/height</li>
    <li>Not accounting for metabolic adaptation</li>
    <li>Expecting perfect precision (10–15% error is normal)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Using TDEE for weight goals</h2>
  <p><strong>Weight loss:</strong> Subtract 250–500 calories</p>
  <p><strong>Weight gain:</strong> Add 250–500 calories</p>
  <p><strong>Maintenance:</strong> Eat at TDEE exactly</p>
  <p>The <a href="/">calorie calculator</a> automates this with goal selection.</p>

  <h2>TDEE changes with weight</h2>
  <p>Losing weight lowers TDEE:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Lose 5 kg? Drop ~100–150 calories</li>
    <li>Recalculate every 4–5 kg</li>
    <li>Use <a href="/tdee-calculator/">TDEE calculator</a> with updated weight</li>
  </ul>
</ContentLayout>